From: Fathom <fathom@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] library: static libraries as code for an executable

Fathom links mbedTLS's static libraries only into its player, a static
program, and lighttpd uses the shared ones. GCC's MIPS default (-mshared)
is code fit for a shared library, every call and global reached through
the GOT; the static libraries get -mno-shared -mplt (direct calls,
absolute addresses) and a section per function, so the player's
--gc-sections leaves out what it never calls. The shared libraries are
built as before.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Fathom's build choice]

--- a/library/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/library/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -306,6 +306,14 @@
     add_library(${mbedtls_static_target} STATIC ${src_tls})
     set_target_properties(${mbedtls_static_target} PROPERTIES OUTPUT_NAME mbedtls)
     target_link_libraries(${mbedtls_static_target} PUBLIC ${libs} ${mbedx509_static_target})
+
+    # The static libraries are linked only into Fathom's player, a static
+    # program: code for an executable (direct calls, absolute addresses
+    # instead of the GOT), one function per section for its --gc-sections.
+    # The shared ones (lighttpd's) stay as they were.
+    foreach(target ${mbedcrypto_static_target} ${mbedx509_static_target} ${mbedtls_static_target})
+        target_compile_options(${target} PRIVATE -mno-shared -mplt -ffunction-sections -fdata-sections)
+    endforeach()

     if(GEN_FILES)
         add_dependencies(${mbedcrypto_static_target}
